POEM3 = ("Grandfather's compound (unseen poem)",
         "The compound is quiet now;\n"
         "the cock that used to argue with the dawn\n"
         "has gone the way of all proud things,\n"
         "and the mango tree, older than my father's father,\n"
         "drops its fruit for no one.\n\n"
         "Grandfather sits where the shade is thickest,\n"
         "counting the years on the beads of his cap,\n"
         "each bead a season, each season a face\n"
         "that has left for Lagos, for London, for the grave.\n\n"
         "'You will come back,' he tells me,\n"
         "and it is not a question.\n"
         "The mango tree drops another fruit.\n"
         "Somewhere a phone is ringing in a city\n"
         "that does not know his name.")
DRAMA = ("Extract from a play (unseen)",
         "MAMA RISI: (sweeping furiously) Twenty years I have sold pepper in this market. Twenty years! And now a boy "
         "with a clipboard tells me my stall is 'unauthorised'.\n"
         "SEGUN: (not looking up from his phone) Mama, it is the new council policy. Everybody has to register.\n"
         "MAMA RISI: Register! Did I register to be born? Did your father register before he died and left me with "
         "four children and this broom?\n"
         "SEGUN: (quietly) Mama...\n"
         "MAMA RISI: (stopping, staring at the broom) When they demolish this stall, Segun, what will I be? Tell me. "
         "A woman with a broom and no floor to sweep.\n"
         "SEGUN: (putting the phone away at last) They will not demolish it. I filled the form for you last week. "
         "(He produces a folded paper.) Stall number forty-one. Your name. Twenty years, it says here, under "
         "'experience'.\n"
         "(MAMA RISI takes the paper. She does not read it. She holds it against her chest and resumes sweeping, "
         "slowly now.)")

